summary:
LuniMartian Atlas finds the best places on Earth for a test of Moon or Mars work.
Open the tool: https://spaceapps2026.researchedtechnologies.org/
See the demo video: https://spaceapps2026.researchedtechnologies.org/demo/lunimartian-atlas-demo.mp4

A scientist selects one of the 16 candidate lunar regions that NASA studied, or one of 57 Mars sites. Then the scientist types or pastes an experiment brief. AI models on our own server change the brief into conditions in 10 categories. They never name a place or give a figure.

The Atlas then ranks 16,184 areas with a match percent. For each area, it shows what a field team must know:
- the distance to an airfield and a road;
- the human influence and the hazards;
- the cloud, and the power from the Sun and the wind;
- the land status and whom to ask for a permit;
- the hours and the dates with the low Sun of the lunar region.

Our Sun code agrees with NASA JPL Horizons: the median difference is 0.009 hours in a ten-day period.
